age, inline-first for text sinks, so one spec can carry a rich descriptionFile and a short inline description without either sink getting the wrong one."}, {"id": "docs_api_specs_remark_callout", "label": "remark-callout (hand-rolled GitHub-alert mdast transform)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api-specs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_specs_disable_an_api", "label": "Disable an API (disabled: true, never delete)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api-specs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filtering once at the API_SPECS export removes the endpoint from every surface with no other edit; the researched data survives and re-enabling is one word. Build guards fail loudly on dangling inbound references because a half-removed endpoint is exactly the drift they exist to catch."}, {"id": "docs_api_specs_data_provenance_caveat", "label": "Spec data provenance caveat", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api-specs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Some response shapes were seeded from curated samples rather than live JS-rendered portal pages \u2014 treat as best-effort and reconcile against live calls."}, {"id": "docs_api_specs_descriptionfile_endpoint_notes", "label": "descriptionFile endpoint notes (src/content/docs/endpoints/*.md)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api-specs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Long/rich descriptions live as real markdown files to keep api-specs.ts lean; MDX is excluded from that folder so the files load as raw text, not compiled components."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_api_specs_api_specs_layer", "target": "docs_ai_agent_platform_ai_